WEBVTT

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.250
Good afternoon.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.220
Welcome.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.760
Oh, Brother!

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.820
Um, where's Misaki?

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:21.330
Oh, she doesn't feel very 
well, so she took the day off.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.350
I see...

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.850
Brother, it seems like we'd be 
better off going home today.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:27.620
Okay.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.430
Dad!

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.830
Mom!!

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.770
Can you believe it? The day of the regional 
tournament was the anniversary of her parents' deaths.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.990
<i>Naturally</i> she couldn't make it!

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:51.760
Yeah...

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:55.620
Imagine constantly remembering 
even the sad things...

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.700
Possessing a great memory 
can be hard, too, huh?

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:04.290
Yeah. And I kept going on about how 
fantastic her memory was, without thinking...

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:08.590
I was no different, crowing about using 
her memory as a weapon for the team!

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:11.090
And here I thought Misaki 
was being irresponsible

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.190
for getting to the regional 
tournament late...

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.130
What should we do?

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:18.000
A-Anyway, right now, we have 
to think about the nationals!

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.670
If we don't convince Misaki to participate...

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:25.350
But she hasn't been in the store 
since then! What should we...

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.850
Is this the reason you interrupted my nap?

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.520
Excuse me?!

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:35.360
Sorry! I thought maybe you would 
have some idea what to do, Kai...

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.790
And you were takin' a nap, 
without a care in the world!

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:38.680
She should quit.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.320
Anybody who wants to quit should quit.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.270
Kai...?

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:46.420
<i>Everyone</i> has a past.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:50.830
Using that as a perpetual reason for your 
own weakness is childish, pure and simple.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:55.290
W-Why, you...! You don't 
have to put it like that!

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.960
Can't you worry about Misaki 
at least a little bit!

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.660
She's our teammate, isn't she?!

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.550
What's with that guy?!

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.030
Kai...

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:15.000
Beyond Memories

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:19.880
I'm home.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.580
Welcome back, Aichi!

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:22.260
Thanks...

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.950
This is early for you, isn't it?

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:27.780
With the nationals coming up, I thought 
you'd be at Card Capital and not get home...

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.710
'til... later...

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.290
Aichi?

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.380
Did something happen?

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.730
I don't know...

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.260
Emi? Where are you going?

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.740
There we go!

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:53.250
Misaki! Help me set out 
the new cards, please!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.740
Please!

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.290
No dice?

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:03.360
What should we do, Manager?

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:09.090
Congratulations, Q4, on Making the National Tournament!

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:08.550
All I can do is watch over her.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:11.600
I don't know what to do...

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.120
No-no! Don't do that, Sub-manager!

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.420
I mean, "Manager"...

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:26.210
They're here! The new packs 
and constructed decks!

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:27.150
Hello...

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.510
Yes, welcome?

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.390
Is Misaki here?

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.730
Misaki!

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:40.850
Emi...

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:42.510
What's wrong?

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.000
Um...

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.260
I don't know if it's okay ask 
you this or not, Misaki, but...

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.240
A question? What is it?

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.620
Aichi is feeling down.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:56.250
Even though he's been all excited about 
the national tournament up until now.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.420
Oh, really?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.910
I thought maybe something had 
happened with the team...

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.390
Have you heard anything, Misaki?

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:06.920
No, nothing.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:08.860
I see...

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.250
Sorry for bothering you.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:15.600
Well, since you came all this 
way, please stay a while.

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:18.850
The new cards just came in!

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:20.650
New cards?!

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.910
Meteo Break Wizard...

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:24.940
Goddess of Flower Divination, Sakuya...

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.730
Sword Dancer, Angel...

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.140
Dark Cat...

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:29.770
Battle Sister, Maple...

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:31.280
Victory Maker...

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.710
These two cards are cute!

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.150
Right, Misaki?!

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.430
Uh-huh...

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:39.830
I wonder what kind of fight 
you can have with them...

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.300
Would you like to give it a try?

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.010
Sure!

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:43.130
You heard her!

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:44.550
Me...?

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:48.390
Sorry, but right now, 
I'm really not in the...

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:50.220
Let's do it, Misaki!

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:59.320
This'll work as a fighting table for today!

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.890
Misaki, where's your deck?

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:05.600
I can't...

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:10.830
I can't fight together 
with you guys anymore...

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.220
Shin, I...

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:21.240
Your deck has been stored safely.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.630
But more importantly, these!

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:23.960
Ta-daa!

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:25.850
A new deck?!

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:26.880
A constructed deck?

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.680
That's right.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:29.210
Here you are.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:32.380
Emi has an Oracle Thinktank deck.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:34.880
Misaki, you get a Nova Grappler deck.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:37.070
What's a "constructed deck"?

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:40.180
A deck that anyone can use 
to play Cardfight right away.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:43.980
But decks take time to 
put together, don't they?

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:48.030
It <i>does</i> take time to put 
together constructed decks.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:53.090
Each card is put in there with love, so 
even the first-time player can have fun.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:54.990
With love?

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:03.970
Misaki?

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:06.070
Okay, you've reviewed the cards?

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:07.700
I'll take the empty boxes.

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:11.730
It's nothing.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.420
Well, shall we start?

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:14.750
Yeah!

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:28.440
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.340
I'll start.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.960
I ride Oasis Girl!

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.350
Battleraizer moves to the rear-guard.

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:41.750
My turn ends.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.130
It's my turn!

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:48.380
I ride Battle Sister, Maple!

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.210
Lozenge moves back.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.750
And then...

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:57.590
I call the Black Kitty!

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:02.020
I-It's "Dark Cat", not Black Kitty...

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.730
Well, it <i>is</i> a black kitty...

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.280
Pink doggy!

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.780
That's Flogal, Misaki.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.800
Flogal...

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:20.830
Next, I attack!

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:21.590
Wait...

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:28.300
When Dark Cat comes into play, if there's an 
Oracle Thinktank unit in the Vanguard Circle...

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:31.610
each Fighter gets to draw a card.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.000
I see...

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:38.860
I attack Oasis Girl with Dark Cat!

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:44.370
Damage check.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.890
Maple attacks!

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.740
I guess I don't have enough power...

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:52.530
It's okay.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:58.110
When Maple attacks, if you have four or more 
cards in your hand, you get +3000 power.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.200
I see!

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:04.330
Drive check!

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:07.960
Damage check.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:12.030
Has she already memorized the 
cards that came in stock...

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:13.860
that <i>I</i> don't even remember yet?

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:16.440
Just what I'd expect from you, Misaki.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:19.520
That's the end of my turn! You're up, Misaki.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:24.970
But there's something that I 
really want you to remember.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:26.870
It's my turn.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:30.700
I ride Super Electromagnetic Lifeform, Storm.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:35.480
Then I call Prototype, 
Minotaur, and Oasis Girl.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:39.370
Uh, excuse me. Would you 
mind getting off of that?

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.790
Manager...

00:10:57.140 --> 00:11:00.840
I attack with Sword Dancer, 
Angel, boosted by Dark Cat!

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.020
I guard with Cannon Ball!

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:09.220
Then, I, uh...

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:13.940
Sorry. After you came out for me...

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:17.440
I attack one more time, 
with a boost from Lozenge!

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.620
Drive check!

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.250
Damage check.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:34.710
Awww, Lozenge left...

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:38.500
Come to think of it, last time 
you didn't use Lozenge's skill

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.540
because you didn't want to put 
her back in the deck, right?

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:42.830
Yeah, but it was frustrating!

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.810
I can see that.

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:47.760
When your attack doesn't hit, 
it <i>is</i> frustrating, isn't it?

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.810
Then I'll stand and draw.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.790
I ride Death Metal Droid!

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:59.150
I move Battling Minotaur 
back and call Storm.

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:03.670
NGM Prototype is boosted by Battleraizer...

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:06.030
and attacks Sword Dancer, Angel!

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:12.530
When Battleraizer gives a boost, the 
unit receives another +3000 power.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:23.020
And then Death Metal attacks, 
boosted by Oasis Girl!

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.720
Certainly, Death Metal...

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:27.470
Counterblast.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.680
+3000 power!

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:32.280
Then its power is 20000!

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:37.200
The shields of these three cards aren't 
enough to help me here, are they?

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:39.820
Twin drive, first check...

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:43.430
Second check...

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:45.200
Stand trigger activated.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:50.070
I choose one unit to give +5000 power to.

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:53.230
I choose Storm, who isn't 
finished attacking yet.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:58.720
And then, this unit which has finished attacking...

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:01.000
What will Emi draw...?

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.880
Damage trigger...

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:10.250
Here I go! I attack your Sword Dancer 
with Storm, boosted by Minotaur!

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.780
I activate Storm's skill!

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:20.100
When your opponent's Vanguard 
is hit with an attack...

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:23.180
you can flip over one card 
that's in the Damage Zone.

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.530
Are you done?

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:25.490
Not yet.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:26.800
This, from before...

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.240
I attack your Sword Dancer with Prototype!

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:36.210
Um... I guard with Dream Eater!

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.520
Well done!

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:45.260
Misaki isn't holding back 
at all on Emi today...

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:46.560
End phase.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:50.140
I'm returning Battleraizer 
to the deck and shuffling.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:52.730
Are you surprised?

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:58.390
I already think of you as a 
full-fledged Cardfighter, Emi...

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:00.860
so going easy on you would 
be rude, wouldn't it?

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:02.720
Uh-huh!

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:05.630
I didn't really understand it until now,

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.740
but this is a lot of fun!

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.200
Fun...

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.460
Are you having fun, Misaki?

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:18.730
Is it fun looking at the cards, Misaki?

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:21.490
Uh-huh! There are so many cards!

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:24.440
Misaki says she remembers all of the cards.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:26.210
She has a good memory!

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:28.210
She must take after me!

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:29.680
She takes after <i>me</i>!

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:31.270
It's <i>me</i>, I say!

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:34.900
Honey, you can't even remember 
the shop's phone number!

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:38.400
And in the car, if I don't navigate from 
the passenger's seat, you always get lost!

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.270
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:45.730
There they go again!

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:47.310
Go! Go! Manager!

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:48.860
Fight, lady!

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:49.900
Don't call me "lady"!

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:55.490
This month, Mom has 45 
wins and Dad has 14 wins!

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:59.550
At least try to win half the time, uncle!

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:00.960
Call me "Manager"!

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:09.300
What...was <i>that</i>...?

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.530
Mom and Dad were laughing...

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:17.620
And so was I...

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:23.240
Um...

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:25.840
When this unit comes into play,

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:30.610
all of your Oracle Thinktank units in 
the rear-guard return to your hand...

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:34.200
I ride Goddess of Flower Divination, Sakuya!

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:37.030
And then these two cards go to my hand.

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:41.460
Then I call two Sword Dancer, 
Angels and a Black Kitty!

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:46.330
When Black Kitty... I mean 
"Dark Cat"... comes into play,

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:50.300
if an Oracle Thinktank unit is 
my Vanguard, I can draw one card!

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:53.590
I activate Sword Dancer, Angel's skill!

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:57.230
When I draw a card, her 
power increases by +1000!

00:15:57.230 --> 00:16:00.080
I call Gemini and Weather Girl, Milk!

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:06.750
Dark Cat gives a boost!

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.570
I attack with Sword Dancer!

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.970
I guard with Ring Girl, Clara!

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.620
Then Sakuya next!

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:19.940
Milk's boost puts her 
power up to 16000, right?

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:25.600
Twin drive check!

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.650
First, second...

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.550
Damage check!

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:34.960
I attack one more time with Sword Dancer!

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.100
I guard with Battleraizer!

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:43.060
Ah! I couldn't do more than 1 damage!

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:45.500
Not at all! That's really something.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:51.180
Keep learning, and you'll become 
quite the Vanguard Fighter!

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.280
Really?!

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:57.060
I wonder if I'll ever be as good as Misaki...

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:03.410
I wonder if I'll ever be as good 
a Vanguard Fighter as you, Dad...

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:04.860
Oh, sure you will!

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:08.720
In fact, you may even become 
a lot stronger than me!

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:12.820
The world of Vanguard is such a big 
place, there's no end to the fun!

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:17.390
Misaki, I'm sure you'll also make lots of 
allies and rivals as you discover this wide world...

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.080
Maybe you'll even make it to 
the national championship!

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.420
Oh my gosh!

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:24.240
Everyone at Card Capital will 
have to go there to cheer her on!

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:27.750
I'll make a <i>gigantic</i> banner!

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:29.260
A banner...?

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:31.710
Yeah! A <i>gigantic</i> one! A <i>humongous</i> one!

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:37.900
You want to become a Vanguard 
Fighter like Misaki?

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:40.580
Uh-huh! After all, I can't lose to Aichi!

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:46.550
Before, he was always alone and wouldn't have 
been able to do anything if it weren't for me.

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:51.190
But now he's got a lot of friends and 
is gonna go to the national tournament!

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:53.190
So, me too!

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:58.410
When you put it like that, I know it was 
worth giving you the constructed deck!

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:01.760
I told you, remember?

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:07.990
Every single card is put in there with love, 
so even the first-time player can have fun.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:13.820
My own deck?!

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:19.780
Yep. I put my whole heart into making that 
deck for you, Misaki, every single card.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:21.880
Thank you, Dad!

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.460
It's my... turn...

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:33.550
I call King of Sword.

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:35.320
I drop Prototype.

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:37.140
I call Queen of Heart.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.730
Why...?

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:42.240
The King attacks, boosted by the Queen!

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:44.930
The Queen's skill adds +4000 power!

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.240
I intercept with Sword Dancer!

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:51.740
Everyone, protect Sakuya!

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:59.240
Why did I try not to remember those times...?

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:02.470
I attack with Death Metal!

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:09.690
There they go again!

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:11.310
Go! Go! Manager!

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:12.790
Fight, lady!

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:13.840
Don't call me "lady"!

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:21.510
It's not all sad things...

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:23.240
Twin drive...

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.760
Damage check!

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.270
I attack with Super Electromagnetic 
Lifeform, Storm!

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:32.420
There were fun things, too...

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:35.420
Things I mustn't forget, and yet...

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:39.520
The world of Vanguard is such a big 
place, there's no end to the fun!

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:44.390
Misaki, I'm sure you'll also make lots of 
allies and rivals as you discover this wide world...

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:47.080
Maybe you'll even make it to 
the national championship!

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:51.290
My own deck?!

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:57.340
Yep. I put my whole heart into making that 
deck for you, Misaki, every single card.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:02.230
Oh, too bad!

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:05.270
But I had fun! Thank you, Misaki...

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:08.890
Misaki...?

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:14.240
Misaki...

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:19.240
Shin... I...

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:20.930
That treasure chest...

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:23.800
I don't have a key...

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.230
The deck Dad put together for me...

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:30.140
I can't open the treasure box, so...

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:32.810
What should I do about the key?

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:33.930
Shin!

00:20:36.990 --> 00:20:39.260
You finally remembered, didn't you?

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:42.040
I've been keeping it for you.

00:20:42.810 --> 00:20:45.050
Because it's a valuable 
memory of yours, Misaki.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:49.490
Thank you...

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.690
Kam...I should really...

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:06.450
Brother, it's more <i>my</i> fault...

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:10.140
Right. Misaki is an important friend...

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:12.040
We'll go in and beg...

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:15.370
Misaki, I'm sorry!

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:18.190
Misaki, I didn't think about your feelings!

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:19.300
That goes double for me!

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:22.290
Please! Let's do Vanguard fight together...

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:25.650
You're late!

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:26.430
Huh?

00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:32.390
What is this?!

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:33.850
What happened?

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:35.300
Aichi!

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:38.860
Misaki is amazing! She's 
won all of these fights!

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:42.440
Yeesh. Not one of them was even 
the slightest match for me.

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:45.820
How am I gonna train for 
the nationals at this rate?

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:47.700
You said "nationals"!

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:48.950
Misaki, you mean...

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:51.300
What are you gaping at?

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:53.000
You're next!

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:55.000
S-Sure!

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:56.660
Yesss!

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.380
My pleasure!

00:21:58.380 --> 00:21:59.710
I'm not gonna pull any punches.

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:06.840
Ready?

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:08.220
Uh-huh!

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:10.820
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:53.940
Misaki, please fight me one more time!

00:23:53.940 --> 00:23:56.450
Okay. Today, I'll fight 
you as often as you like.

00:23:56.450 --> 00:23:57.150
Great!

00:23:57.150 --> 00:24:00.660
For the national tournament, we're meeting 
at Card Capital and traveling by car, right?

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:03.960
Right. But don't worry, I've 
memorized how to get there.

00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:07.280
Who needs GPS when all you have 
to do is take one look at a map?

00:24:07.280 --> 00:24:08.420
It's incredible!

00:24:08.420 --> 00:24:10.760
Oh, I'm sorry! Please don't 
take that the wrong way!

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:14.180
Next: A Stormy Beginning! 
The National Championship!

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:16.350
I can only imagine the 
new people we'll meet...

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:18.780
Kamui, it's dangerous to 
run around like that!
